// ── type ref kinds (NAMES-1b): the type namespace is separate from the value namespace (s2/names.srs Names.Ns 97: an enum and its
// case may share a name). Rules, as s2: a type name is a builtin (Names.builtins7 173, Array/Cell 163, ACell 170), an enum (192),
// a capability (proto 400), a handler (431), a trait (198), a type decl (201) or an extern struct (209, a TypeDecl body); a use is
// a [] binder in scope (Names.tparams 233: enum, trait, type, given, def groups) or else a declared type name (Names.tyIn 255).
// Not in s2, added here: Trait and Handler are kinds of their own (s2 only knows "a type"). ──
enum Resolve.TK:
  case Resolve.TEnum
  case Resolve.TDecl
  case Resolve.TCap
  case Resolve.TBuiltin
  case Resolve.TParam
  case Resolve.TTrait
  case Resolve.THandler
  case Resolve.TUnres

